+# Epic Breakdown: Pulseboard
+
+**Project**: Pulseboard  
+**Date**: 2026-08-10  
+**Total Epics**: 3 (E000 plus 2 product epics)  
+**Estimated Total Stories**: 17–24
+
+## Epic Dependency Map
+
+```text
+E000 Developer Infrastructure
+  └── E001 Safe Proposal Review
+        └── E002 Reminder Delivery and Status
+```
+
+## Epic Prioritization
+
+### MVP Epics
+
+- E000: Developer Infrastructure
+- E001: Safe Proposal Review
+- E002: Reminder Delivery and Status
+
+There are no enhancement or future epics in this plan; the four-week pilot scope is deliberately limited to the product contract.
+
+## Epic Definitions
+
+### E000: Developer Infrastructure
+
+**Value Statement**: This epic enables the team to build and assess the pilot reliably by providing repeatable checks and safe environment conventions.
+
+**Scope Summary**: Establish the minimum delivery foundation for a Python API and browser UI: local test commands, lint/format checks, CI for checks and builds, environment configuration, and structured failure visibility. It does not choose or integrate the reminder provider.
+
+**Success Criteria**:
+
+- [ ] API and browser tests can run locally through documented commands.
+- [ ] CI runs linting, tests, and production build checks on proposed changes.
+- [ ] Environment configuration keeps provider credentials out of source control.
+- [ ] Runtime failures produce actionable structured logs or an equivalent observable failure signal.
+
+**User Stories Summary**:
+
+- Python API and browser UI project/test setup
+- Linting, formatting, and build commands
+- CI pipeline and environment/secrets conventions
+- Structured error and request logging baseline
+
+**Dependencies**:
+
+- **Depends On**: None.
+- **Enables**: E001 and E002.
+
+**Touch-points (creates/modifies)**:
+
+- Migrations: —
+- Models/Services: application configuration, logging, and test support
+- Files/Components: CI workflow, API test suite, browser UI test suite, environment example/documentation
+
+**Estimated Stories**: 4–5  
+**Priority**: P0 — Foundation  
+**Target Phase**: Phase 0
+
+---
+
+### E001: Safe Proposal Review
+
+**Value Statement**: This epic enables meeting facilitators to turn an uploaded transcript into workspace-private, reviewed action items without any action being scheduled before explicit human confirmation.
+
+**Scope Summary**: Deliver the controlled core journey: workspace-scoped transcript upload, extraction of proposed actions, and facilitator review. It establishes the server-side confirmation gate for action text, owner, and due date, as well as the real-request-path authorization boundary. It stops before provider delivery.
+
+**Success Criteria**:
+
+- [ ] A facilitator can upload a transcript and see extracted action proposals in the same workspace.
+- [ ] A facilitator can edit, reject, or explicitly confirm proposal text, owner, and due date.
+- [ ] An action without all three explicit confirmations cannot become delivery-eligible.
+- [ ] A user from another workspace cannot read this workspace's transcript or actions through the real request role.
+- [ ] Review-state records support calculating the proposal review rate.
+
+**User Stories Summary**:
+
+- Workspace membership and request-path authorization boundary
+- Transcript upload, storage, and extraction orchestration
+- Proposal list and action-detail review UI
+- Explicit text/owner/due-date confirmation mechanism
+- Confirmed-action eligibility and review metrics
+- Cross-workspace negative authorization probe
+
+**Dependencies**:
+
+- **Depends On**: E000.
+- **Enables**: E002.
+
+**Touch-points (creates/modifies)**:
+
+- Migrations: workspace membership, transcripts, action proposals/actions, review/confirmation state
+- Models/Services: workspace authorization, transcript ingestion/extraction, proposal review, action eligibility
+- Files/Components: upload screen, proposal-review screen, API request handlers, authorization and workflow tests
+
+**Estimated Stories**: 8–11  
+**Priority**: P0 — Pilot critical  
+**Target Phase**: Phase 1
+
+---
+
+### E002: Reminder Delivery and Status
+
+**Value Statement**: This epic enables facilitators to close the loop on a confirmed action with one configurable reminder and a visible delivery outcome.
+
+**Scope Summary**: Implement a narrow reminder-provider adapter, provider configuration, eligibility-checked delivery, idempotency, and delivery-status presentation. It consumes E001's confirmed actions and must never widen the product into autonomous or repeated outbound messaging.
+
+**Success Criteria**:
+
+- [ ] A configured provider can receive one reminder request for an eligible confirmed action.
+- [ ] Ineligible or unconfirmed actions cannot create a delivery attempt.
+- [ ] Retrying the same single-reminder intent does not create an unintended duplicate delivery.
+- [ ] The facilitator can see delivered, pending, or failed status as reported by the provider.
+- [ ] The runtime path can demonstrate upload-to-confirmation-to-delivery.
+
+**User Stories Summary**:
+
+- Provider adapter contract and configuration
+- Delivery-attempt creation and idempotency guard
+- Provider result handling and status persistence
+- Facilitator delivery-status UI
+- End-to-end workflow and failure-path tests
+
+**Dependencies**:
+
+- **Depends On**: E000 and E001.
+- **Enables**: The complete pilot workflow and required runtime evidence.
+
+**Touch-points (creates/modifies)**:
+
+- Migrations: provider configuration reference and delivery-attempt/status records
+- Models/Services: reminder provider adapter, delivery orchestration, idempotency, status mapping
+- Files/Components: provider configuration surface, delivery-status UI, API handlers, end-to-end and provider-contract tests
+
+**Estimated Stories**: 5–8  
+**Priority**: P0 — Pilot critical  
+**Target Phase**: Phase 2
+
+## Epic Execution Strategy
+
+### Phase 0: Foundation
+
+**Epic**: E000  
+**Goal**: Make implementation and later proof repeatable before product behavior is added.  
+**Success gate**: local and CI checks cover the API/browser build boundary and environment secrets are not committed.
+
+### Phase 1: Controlled Proposal Workflow
+
+**Epic**: E001  
+**Goal**: Deliver the human-confirmed, workspace-isolated transcript-to-action path.  
+**Success gate**: positive review path and real-request-role negative workspace probe are executable.
+
+### Phase 2: Reminder Closure
+
+**Epic**: E002  
+**Goal**: Add one provider-backed reminder and visible delivery outcome.  
+**Success gate**: the full upload-to-confirmation-to-delivery path is executable for later evidence collection.
+
+## Risk Mitigation by Epic
+
+| Epic | Primary Risk | Mitigation Strategy |
+|---|---|---|
+| E000 | Checks are unavailable or unrepresentative | Establish executable local and CI commands before product work |
+| E001 | Human-control or tenant-isolation promises are cosmetic | Enforce them in API state transitions and request-role tests |
+| E002 | Provider uncertainty or retries cause incorrect sending | Isolate provider behind an adapter and make delivery idempotent/status-visible |
+
+## Success Metrics by Epic
+
+| Epic | Key Metric | Target | Measurement |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| E000 | Core checks runnable in CI | Every proposed change | CI run record |
+| E001 | Proposal review rate and isolation probe | ≥80% review; 0 successful cross-workspace probes | Review-state records and negative probe |
+| E002 | Complete controlled workflow | One visible result per eligible reminder intent | Runtime workflow evidence and delivery records |
+
+## Notes
+
+- This Build-level plan contains two product epics, so the Build 4+ product-epic architecture/UX/analyze gate does not apply.
+- E000 is retained because no existing delivery infrastructure is supplied; there is no evidence that all E000 skip criteria are met.
+- `project-analyze` remains recommended before the first epic is specified.
